{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusDivision","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Span"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.division_of_skew_division","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.division_of_skew_division","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L161-L175","doc":"**The `division` field is exactly brick B3 (PROVED, modulo the B3 gap).**\nWhen `Â`'s top L-coefficient is a unit (the localized-torus condition), the\n`TransferLemmas.division` hypothesis is `exists_skew_right_division`\nspecialised to the divisor `Â`.  So beyond the B1–B3 skew-Laurent infra the\nonly genuinely-new inputs the conditional theorem needs are the\ncorpus-PROVED `aj_mem` and the [Tr4] `minimality` wall.\n\n(This lemma is sorry-free; it *depends on* `exists_skew_right_division`,\nwhich carries the two documented B3 `sorry`s — an honest dependency, per the\ntask's permission to depend on `exists_skew_right_division`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.strong_aj_figure_eight_of_transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.strong_aj_figure_eight_of_transfer","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L141-L159","doc":"**Strong AJ for the figure eight — ideal generation (Theorem, CONDITIONAL on\nthe [Tr4] transfer lemmas).**  The recurrence ideal `A_{4₁} = I` is the\nprincipal left ideal generated by the AJ operator `Â`:\n`I = Ideal.span {Â}`.\n\nDERIVED from the class fields via `principal_of_division_minimality` — a real\ncomposition of the three inputs, **not** a projection of the conclusion.\nFully Lean-verified modulo the single class instance, which is *not* provided\nhere (the honest \"open\" state): `aj_mem` is corpus-PROVED-but-untranslated,\n`division` inherits the two B3 `sorry`s, `minimality` is the [Tr4] wall.\n\nPer the anti-laundering rule this is a *rigorous conditional result*, NOT a\nclaim that strong AJ is proved in Lean.\n-- Ref: [nguyen-tran-2021] Theorem 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.minimality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.minimality","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L139-L139","doc":"`Â` is the minimal-order annihilator ([Tr4, Lemmas 3.1–3.3]). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.division","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.division","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L136-L136","doc":"Skew-Euclidean right-division by `Â` (brick B3 `exists_skew_right_division`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.aj_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.aj_mem","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L134-L134","doc":"`Â` annihilates the tower — it lies in the recurrence ideal.\n(Corpus-PROVED `figureEightOperator_annihilates`, translated.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas.mk","kind":"ctor","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.TransferLemmas","kind":"class","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L114-L139","doc":"**[Tr4] transfer inputs for figure-eight strong-AJ generation (§3b-cond\nclass).**  The three genuine INPUTS Nguyen–Tran compose to prove Theorem 1\nat the ideal level, for a left ideal `I` (the recurrence ideal `A_{4₁}`) and\nthe AJ operator `Aop` (`Â`):\n\n* `aj_mem` — `Â` annihilates the colored Jones tower (`Â ∈ I`).  This is the\n  corpus-PROVED `figureEightOperator_annihilates`, translated to the torus.\n* `division` — right-division by `Â` in the localized torus terminates with a\n  strictly-smaller-`topDeg` remainder (brick B3).\n* `minimality` — `Â` is the minimal-order annihilator: every element of `I`\n  of smaller `topDeg` is `0`.  This is the paper's cited [Tr4, Lemmas\n  3.1–3.3] transfer input.\n\nNone of these fields is the conclusion `I = span {Â}`; each is a genuine\nsub-hypothesis, so the downstream theorem is non-degenerate (§3b-cond item 5,\n`proof-statement-integrity`).\n-- Ref: [nguyen-tran-2021] Theorem 1, Lemmas 2.1–2.2; [Tr4] = arXiv:1404.0331. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.principal_of_division_minimality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.StrongAJFigureEight.principal_of_division_minimality","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/StrongAJFigureEight.lean#L78-L112","doc":"**Principal generation from division + minimality (PROVED — the Euclidean\ncore).**  Let `I` be a left ideal of the quantum torus containing `a`.  If\nright-division by `a` always leaves a strictly-smaller-`topDeg` remainder,\nand `a` is the minimal-degree nonzero element of `I` (every element of `I`\nof smaller `topDeg` vanishes), then `I` is the principal left ideal\n`span {a}`.\n\nThis is the genuine mathematical content of \"the recurrence ideal is\nprincipal\": any `P ∈ I` reduces mod `a` to a remainder `r ∈ I` of smaller\ndegree, which minimality kills, so `P = q·a`.  It **derives** the conclusion\nby composing the two hypotheses — it does not assume it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}